{"name":"Habañero","hex":"#f98513","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"habañero","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(hypercorrect) Nonstandard form of habanero."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/haba%C3%B1ero"}],"entries":[{"title":"Habanero","blocks":[{"text":"The habanero is a pungent cultivar of Capsicum chinense chili pepper. Unripe habaneros are green, and they color as they mature. The most common color variants are orange and red, but the fruit may also be white, brown, yellow, green, or purple. Typically, a ripe habanero is 2–6 centimetres long. Habanero chilis are very hot, rated 100,000–350,000 on the Scoville scale. The habanero's heat, flavor, and floral aroma make it a common ingredient in hot sauces and other spicy foods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Habanero_closeup_edit2.jpg/330px-Habanero_closeup_edit2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Habanero","wikidata":"Q764375"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/ExpoIndigenous2015_065.JPG/500px-ExpoIndigenous2015_065.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/ExpoIndigenous2015_065.JPG/1280px-ExpoIndigenous2015_065.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/ExpoIndigenous2015_065.JPG/500px-ExpoIndigenous2015_065.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Habanero hot sauce from Flor de Lirio, an Indigenous cooperative in Peto Municipality, Yucatán","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AExpoIndigenous2015_065.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Habanero_cut_in_half_on_a_blue_plate.jpg/500px-Habanero_cut_in_half_on_a_blue_plate.jpg?utm_so